job_description_text:
**Middle/Senior Python Developer**

**For now we are looking for candidates only from Romania :)**
We are an R&D and consultancy business focused on solutions in fintech, edutech, healthtech, e-commerce, IoT, AI/robotics and blockchain. The company is serving customers from three continents - Asia, Europe and America.

We are building solutions for various industries by using the best engineering practices, cutting edge technologies and the latest tools.

From identifying the suitable technologies to integrating with the best already built solutions, our focus is to help our customers to reduce costs, improve quality and come up with the best long-term scalable products.

We are looking for a Middle/Senior Python Developer to join our team.


**Project:**

Family social networking application. It is a location-based service designed primarily to enable friends and family members to share their location with each other. 
Known for first-to-market solutions for modern family challenges, we recently reached #1 in Apple’s US App Store’s list of free social networking apps. Nearly 1 in 10 US families with kids use our application an average of 12 times a day, and global membership is growing exponentially, with over 33 million active users in over 195 countries as of late 2021 — making our product  the largest mobile service for families in the world. 

**Responsibilities:**

● Implementing high complexity solutions and improve existing features and code
maintainability;
● Delivering complex and high-quality software solutions (standalone or integrated with
the existing products);
● Working in an agile environment;
● Collaborate with team and product manager to achieve and extend the overall vision of
the project;
● Perform peer review and peer programming;
● Implement solutions based on requirements in an estimated timeframe;
● Implement unit and integration tests;
● Solve reported issues.


**Qualifications:**

● 2+ years of software development experience in one or more purpose programming
languages such as Python;
● Good knowledge in at least one popular Python framework (like Django, Flask);
● Knowledge of Python data manipulation libraries (pandas, numpy);
● Hands-on experience in making algorithms production-ready and deploying them in
cloud services;
● Manage the infrastructure and data pipelines needed to bring code to production;
● Experience with SQL databases (Postgres);
● Ability to integrate multiple data sources and databases into one system;
● Familiarity with front-end technologies (like JavaScript);
● Proficient understanding of code versioning tools (such as GitLab, GitHub).


**Recruitment process:**

● HR call (up to 15 minutes) 
● TI: coding challenge (up to 1,5 hour)


**Benefits:**
● Remote/hybrid/office in Bucharest - you choose;
● Medical Insurance at Signal Iduna;
● Paid vacations, paid sick leaves;
● Access to Udemy and Coursera;
● Access to Bookster;
● Christmas Bonus;
● Self-determined career advancement opportunities with training and certification.

