Our Israel-based client has built an **AI-powered research engine**, capable of finding complex patterns in data by understanding their meaning. Operating on the intersection of Data Science and Artificial Intelligence fields, their Machine Learning technology is so ground-breaking that it’s been referred to as science fiction on multiple occasions.

In our model, you’ll interact with your Israeli counterparts directly, while working alongside our merry band of Beetroots in Ukraine.

**Responsibilities**

— Develop and manage all application environments, production, QA & more;
— Manage CD\CI pipeline;
— Manage database platforms – MySql, ArangoDB, ElasticSearch;
— Create and manage a monitoring service;
— Create and manage a backup service & DRP;
— Collaborate with back-end developers and product managers to improve usability;
— Provide second-tier technical support with customer production issues.

**What we’re looking for**

— At least 2 years of experience as a DevOps engineer; 
— Experience with Python;
— Experience with JavaScript;
— Linux fluency;
— Familiarity with MySql, ElasticSearch, Docker, Jenkins or an ability to learn the missing parts quickly;
— A capacity for constant learning;
— Understanding that users come first, as they are the engine of our business;
— Good level of English (both spoken and written).

**Bonus**

— Experience in working within a fast-paced environment; 
— You love borsch!

**Does this describe you?**

There is such a thing as being a “true Beetroot”.

We value people who are eager for continual improvement. Someone who desires to be the most caring, professional, and progressive version of yourself. Your skills and experience are important factors, but your personality, approach, and drive for improvement are what truly make a difference. Our hope is that you will be a team player who can accept responsibility for your work, solve problems pragmatically, and remain highly motivated. It is also important to be outgoing, well-organized, and efficient with a strong ability to prioritize.

Now that we’ve covered the basics, let’s share more about us!

**About Beetroot**

We are a Swedish-Ukrainian IT company, building dream teams of developers and designers for companies around the globe. As an emerging company, co-producing with other emerging companies, we work with both start-up businesses and advanced businesses. In essence, we are the cannonball for our client’s success. With over 400 team members, Beetroot fosters a family environment. We are a tightly knit group who loves spending time together. Our desire is to provide a cozy workplace full of trust, equality, and steamy bowls of borsch!

**Do you like perks? So do we! We provide:**
— A work environment with a minimum level of hierarchy
— Family-like culture in a comfortable, well-equipped office
— Great networking opportunities with international clients
— Personal and professional development opportunities
— Competitive salary, paid vacation, medical insurance, and social benefits
— Team building activities: ski trips, Beetroot breakfast, movie nights...and more!
— English lessons with native speakers
— Discounted Beetroot Academy courses
— Annual allowance to participate in competence-enhancing events

**Are you a good fit? Send us your CV in English. We are waiting to hear from you!**

Our Israel-based client has built an **AI-powered research engine**, capable of finding complex patterns in data by understanding their meaning. Operating on the intersection of Data Science and Artificial Intelligence fields, their Machine Learning technology is so ground-breaking that it’s been referred to as science fiction on multiple occasions.

In our model, you’ll interact with your Israeli counterparts directly, while working alongside our merry band of Beetroots in Ukraine.

**Responsibilities**

— Develop and manage all application environments, production, QA & more;
— Manage CD\CI pipeline;
— Manage database platforms – MySql, ArangoDB, ElasticSearch;
— Create and manage a monitoring service;
— Create and manage a backup service & DRP;
— Collaborate with back-end developers and product managers to improve usability;
— Provide second-tier technical support with customer production issues.

**What we’re looking for**

— At least 2 years of experience as a DevOps engineer; 
— Experience with Python;
— Experience with JavaScript;
