Join us!

We are looking for an experienced Full-stack engineer to join our professional team. The client is a UK-based market-leading hardware manufacturer in the tech industry which help deliver a bespoke solution to global inventory management.

**We expect from you:**
● Must be highly qualified in C# – this is a screening prerequisite;
● Experience with SQL is required;
● Experience with unit testing is required;
● Experience with SSRS (SQL Server Reporting Services) is highly desirable;
● Experience with Visual Basic on the .NET framework is highly desirable.

**Candidates must be located in Europe Economic Area (EEA) or US or South Africa or Turkey**

**As a Full-stack Engineer, you will:**
● Develop the product to meet the defined user stories;
● Provide insight and best practices for approaching technical problems;
● Attend and support the relevant sprint ceremonies;
● Write and execute unit tests;
● Conduct handovers to QA and support QA with user demos;
● Create documentation of features developed;
● Adhere to coding standards and development processes.

**Stack:**
● MS Azure, Amazon ECS, C# VB.Net, SQL, SSRS.

**Assessment stages:**
● HR interview;
● Technical assessment looking at Tech questions related to stack (20-30mins);
● Code test live (40-60mins);
● Interview with the client (1hr)

**We offer:**
● full remote with flexible business hours (from 8:00 to 20:00);
● 3 weeks of vacation per year (15 working days);
● paid sick leave per year (5 working days);
● amazing opportunities for professional growth within a top-notch team of professionals;
● competitive compensation commensurate with your experience and skills;
● English lessons;
● an excellent team with a friendly atmosphere.

