job_description_text:
In this role, you will be responsible for analyzing the functionality of applications and designing and building automated tools and tests to validate the CICD regression for quality and performance. You will be required to work closely with the developers to build together automation for maximum coverage. To ensure success as an Automation Engineer, you should have advanced programming skills, deep knowledge of testing frameworks and tools, a keen eye for detail, and an excellent end to end understanding of the product and platform.

Key responsibilities :

Work closely with the developers and build automation tools/frameworks/best practices to enable the developers fastly develop automation for the components they are developing
Build automation solution for end to end regression testing, incorporating UI and backend
Develop automation test plans for maximum regression coverage
Identifying and measuring software application weaknesses and target areas, and automating tests accordingly.

Requirements :

3+ years in planning & developing test automation solution for high scale platforms
BOTH UI automation and backend automation
Building automation for big data systems — automating data pipelines
Testing using REST APIs and APIs automation
Building UI Automation frameworks (such as Cypress / Selenium)
Planning functional end to end test plans
Working on complex platform — front end / back end and micro services

Bonus points :

Experience in working with Cloud environment (GCP preferred)
Experience in working with K8S

We offer :

Stable employment within an international, well-established, fast-growing company;
A great, diverse and inclusive work environment with many social opportunities both inside and outside work;
Fast hiring process and interesting vacancies;
The atmosphere is built on trust, support, and mutual respect;
Competitive, performance-based salary with regular reviews;
Team-building events and fun activities;
Leadership program;
English classes;
PE support by professional accountants;

candidate_cv_text:
Java. Automotive domain. 
Analyzing requirements, coding, taking part in code review, executing and analyzing results of test cases. 
Evaluating existing test cases to detect weaknesses and how to fix. 
Developing and maintaining a test environment -  Jenkins on AWS.
Creating a report and releases notes. 
Creating tools to make my work easier and faster. 
Communication with different development teams, product owner, devops team, customers.

Java 8, Java Collection Framework;
Jenkins, Groovy( only as Jenkins DSL);
Understanding of SDLC;
Solid skill in analysis, decision ­making, and problem-solving;    
Experience in Agile practices and methodologies (SCRUM, Kanban);    
Testing desktop and web-based applications; 
2 years as test engineer, 4 years as General QA( manual + automation)
ISTQB® Certified Tester, Foundation Leve: 16-CTFL-91323-03;
I'm in Odesa now, going to relocate Kyiv.
Looking for a QA Automation position Well organized processes, professional growth, project, that could help to learn new and improve current skills.

