I'm in Odesa now, going to relocate Kyiv.
Looking for a QA Automation position Well organized processes, professional growth, project, that could help to learn new and improve current skills.

I am a qualified QA Engineer with more than seven years of commercial experience, including three years as a company's QA Lead.
I also have experience in Automation testing using Python/Selenium, and I want to improve and use this part of my knowledge.  
In addition, my career allowed me to gain valuable experience as a Project Manager. I can apply my knowledge and expertise to enhance QA performance, establish new QA processes, and contribute to overall organizational success.



Main tech-skills:
- Experience in Software Testing, Manual testing of mobile and web applications;
- Experience with Automation (Python/Selenium WebDriver);
- Knowledge of CI and Docker;
- Establishment of all possible QA processes from scratch;
- Skilled in requirement analysis, test planning, and test cases;
- Skilled in API testing (Charles proxy, Git, Postman, Swagger);
- Knowledge of SQL, XML, HTTP;
- Ability to analyze and report test progress and results using test management tools;
- Experience in the payment system (Stripe);
- Working experience with Performance testing (JMeter);
- Knowledge of SDLC (Waterfall, Agile)


Additional skills:
Experience as Project Manager;
Conducting a technical interview with candidates (from junior to senior levels);
Developing Professional Development Plans  for mentees;
Organizing performance review;
Regular communication with the customer

